      "observed": "FCC1's HSE crystal HSE1 is connected to PE6 (pin 5) and PE7 (pin 37) instead of the dedicated HSE pins PH0 (pin 12) and PH1 (pin 13). NAVC1's HSE crystal HSE2 is not connected to any NAVC1 pin at all; its pins are on nets HSE_IN_NAVC and HSE_OUT_NAVC which have no MCU nodes. NAVC1's PH0 and PH1 are instead tied to 2.2u capacitors to ground.",
      "expected": "The 25 MHz HSE crystals should be connected between the PH0 and PH1 pins of each MCU, with appropriate load capacitors, as required by the STM32H753 and STM32F405 datasheets and the specification's 'HSE crystal (both MCUs)' entry.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"31\") (name \"HSE_IN_FCC\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"C32\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"PE6\") (pintype \"bidirectional\")) (node (ref \"HSE1\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"32\") (name \"HSE_IN_NAVC\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"C52\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"HSE2\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "HSE crystal (both MCUs) | FCC / NAVC | ABM8G-25.000MHZ-4Y-T3"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Neither MCU can use its external 25 MHz crystal. They may fail to start or run at an incorrect frequency, making the board non-functional.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "missing_component",
      "components": ["CH330"],
      "pins": [],
      "nets": [],
      "observed": "The netlist contains no components with value or part 'CH330'. The Connections sheet includes USB connectors USB1–USB4 but no USB-UART bridge ICs.",
      "expected": "Two CH330 USB-UART bridge ICs should be present, as stated in the specification: 'USB-UART bridges (programming/debug) | Connections | otter_CH330 ×2'.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "USB-UART bridges (programming/debug) | Connections | otter_CH330 ×2"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"USB1\") (value \"USB_B_Micro\") ... ) (comp (ref \"USB2\") (value \"USB_B_Micro\") ... ) (comp (ref \"USB3\") (value \"USB_B_Micro\") ... ) (comp (ref \"USB4\") (value \"USB_B_Micro\") ... )"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The intended USB-to-UART programming/debug interface is missing, so the board cannot be programmed or debugged via USB in the specified manner.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain multiple severe anomalies: both MCUs have unconnected power pins, the HSE crystals are miswired or disconnected, and the two specified CH330 USB-UART bridges are missing. These deviations would prevent the board from powering up, running at the correct clock frequency, and being programmed via USB."
}

